--! Fibers: functions that may wait, running side by side
--! (`transparent-effects-proposal.md` §16).
--!
--! A beni function that may wait for something — a timer, a network reply,
--! another fiber — is written like any other function. The compiler infers
--! that it may suspend and emits it so that it can stop in the middle and be
--! resumed later; nothing in the source says so. This module is what such
--! functions run on: a fiber is one line of execution, and many fibers take
--! turns on one JavaScript thread.
--!
--! **Structured.** A fiber started with `spawn` belongs to the fiber that
--! started it and is cancelled when that one ends; one started in a `scope`
--! belongs to the scope and is cancelled, and waited for, when the scope's
--! function returns. Nothing a fiber starts outlives what started it unless
--! it is joined first.
--!
--! **Cancellation is prompt and cleanup is guaranteed.** A fiber that is
--! waiting when it is cancelled stops waiting at once; the release of every
--! `bracket` it is inside runs, last first, before `cancel` returns.
--! Cancellation is delivered only where a fiber may suspend, so a function
--! that never waits is never interrupted in the middle.
--!
--! **A defect ends the program.** There are no exceptions: a failure you
--! expect is a `Result`, and a fiber ends either `Done` with its value or
--! `Cancelled`.

-- The fiber runtime of `transparent-effects-proposal.md` §16.4, whole —
-- the suspension protocol the compiler's output speaks, the fiber record,
-- the scheduler, interruption, finalisers, scopes and the teardown of
-- `boundary.md` §9.8.14 — written in beni over `Js` (`plans/core-in-beni.md`
-- step 2; research 49). No platform is special here; the one host facility
-- it picks by feature is the macrotask it escapes to.
--
-- Three rules make it work (research 49 §0). The runtime's records are
-- `Js.Value`s, one literal each, read and written by name. Every beni
-- function the runtime runs — a fiber's work, a continuation, a finaliser,
-- an observer — is held as a `Js.Value` and called with `Js.apply`, so the
-- checker joins none of them into a function here and none gets a second
-- body. And `Exit` crosses into the records at a type variable (`host`,
-- `guest`), so it pins no tag. A function here is compiled as the plain code
-- it is, handling the sentinel as data, except where it calls one of this
-- module's functions that suspends: there the compiler writes the protocol.
--
-- The protocol (§16.1). A call that parks returns the sentinel, and leaves
-- one pending suspension here: the wait it registered and an empty list of
-- continuations. Each suspendable function the sentinel passes through
-- appends the rest of itself (`andThen`), innermost first, and returns the
-- sentinel in turn, until the fiber's run loop takes the list onto the
-- fiber's stack. A resumption pops one continuation at a time and calls it
-- from the run loop, so a resumed stack is one frame deep. A call that
-- answers with a value continues where it is: the fast path is one
-- comparison.

import Duration exposing (Duration)
import Js
import List
import Schedule exposing (Schedule)


type alias V =
    Js.Value


--| How a fiber ended.
pub type Exit a
    = Done a
    | Cancelled


--| A fiber that is running, or has ended. `join` waits for its value.
pub foreign type Fiber a


--| The fibers a `scope` started. It is cancelled, and waited for, when the
--| scope's function returns.
pub foreign type Scope


--| How a platform's primitive resumes the fiber that waits on it, once: a
--| JavaScript function the platform calls with the value.
pub foreign type Resume a


--| Work queued to run once, in no fiber, where a fiber started now would
--| first run: `soon` makes one, and it is `queued` until it has run.
pub foreign type Soon


-- A beni value seen as a JavaScript one, and back, at a type variable: so
-- the runtime's records and `Exit` pin no field name and no tag
-- (`backend.md` §9, *Item 4, taken up*).
host : a → V
host x = Js.from x


guest : V → a
guest v = Js.to v


-- ---- The protocol ----------------------------------------------------------

-- The one sentinel: an object no beni value can be. It only ever travels
-- between a `return` and the comparison that consumes it.
sentinel : V
sentinel = Js.from { waiting = True }


-- The suspension being unwound, `{ interrupt, ks, wait }`, set by the call
-- that parked and taken by the run loop; null the rest of the time.
pending : Js.Ref V
pending = Js.ref Js.null


--| Used by the code the compiler emits for a function that may suspend, and
--| by nothing else: `andThen value next` is `next value`. Calling it by hand
--| is allowed and does exactly that — which is why it is `impure`: it calls
--| `next` during the call, and `next` may be.
pub andThen : a, sync (a → b) → b
andThen value next =
    if Js.same (Js.from value) sentinel then
        _ = Js.call (Js.get (Js.read pending) "ks") "push" [ Js.from next ]
        Js.to sentinel
    else
        next value


--| Used by the code the compiler emits, and by nothing else: always `False`
--| for any value a program can hold.
pub isWaiting : a → Bool
isWaiting value = Js.same (Js.from value) sentinel


-- Leave the sentinel with a fresh pending suspension: the one place the
-- runtime suspends (`boundary.md` §4.2, `Js.suspending`). `w` is the wait
-- parked on, or null; `intr` that there is no value to go on with.
park : V, Bool → a
park w intr = Js.suspending λ() →
    _ = Js.write pending (Js.from { interrupt = intr, ks = Js.array [], wait = w })
    Js.to sentinel


cancelled : V
cancelled = host Cancelled


-- The fiber whose code is on the JavaScript stack; null outside any fiber
-- (a module being loaded, `main` being evaluated).
current : Js.Ref V
current = Js.ref Js.null


-- Where `spawn`, a finaliser's push and `uninterruptible` act outside any
-- fiber (§16.4): nothing there can park, and nothing runs these finalisers
-- but the teardown. Made on first use.
outside : Js.Ref V
outside = Js.ref Js.null


here : () → V
here () =
    c = Js.read current
    if Js.isNull c then
        o = Js.read outside
        if Js.isNull o then
            f = newFiber Js.null (Js.array [])
            _ = Js.write outside f
            f
        else
            o
    else
        c


-- ---- The fiber's slots (§17.5) ---------------------------------------------

-- Whether any slot has ever been set. Until one has, every fiber's slots
-- are the defaults and nothing is copied; a build that never sets one —
-- every program that uses no clock, log context or seed — folds this to
-- `False`, and its fibers carry no slots and pay nothing for them.
slotted : Js.Ref Bool
slotted = Js.ref False


-- The slots a fiber started from `from` copies: `from`'s own when it is a
-- fiber, the record outside any fiber's when it is null (started outside
-- any), and undefined — every slot at its default — when it is undefined
-- (a platform's root) or there is no such record yet.
slotsOf : V → V
slotsOf from =
    if Js.isUndefined from then
        Js.undefined
    else
        src = if Js.isNull from then Js.read outside else from
        if Js.isNull src then Js.undefined else Js.get src "slots"


-- An interrupt is to be delivered now.
deliverable : V → Bool
deliverable fiber =
    Js.to (Js.get fiber "interrupted")
        && Js.to (Js.get fiber "masks") == 0
        && not (Js.to (Js.get fiber "unwinding"))


-- What a set holds, as an array to walk while the set changes.
copy : V → V
copy set = Js.call (Js.global "Array") "from" [ set ]


-- Whether `spawn` has run: only it gives a fiber children, or work outside
-- any fiber a child of its own. Until it has, no fiber has children to
-- cancel or wait for; a build that never spawns — whose fibers all belong
-- to a scope or are roots — folds this to `False` and keeps none of what
-- looks for them.
spawning : Js.Ref Bool
spawning = Js.ref False


-- Whether a field holding a set or an array holds nothing.
none : V → Bool
none set = Js.isNull set || Js.to (Js.get set "size") == 0


-- ---- The scheduler (§7.5) --------------------------------------------------

-- Ready work, FIFO, as quadruples: the step that runs it and its three
-- arguments. A fiber's is `resumeFiber` with the fiber, the value it resumes
-- with, and the wait that value answers (null for a start or an interrupt);
-- `soon`'s is `runSoon` with its record. A step answers whether it ran: a
-- fiber's whose wait is no longer what the fiber is parked on is stale and
-- does not count. The drain names no step, so a build whose only work is
-- `soon`'s keeps no fiber (`boundary.md` §9.8.11).
queue : V
queue = Js.array []


head : Js.Ref Int
head = Js.ref 0


scheduled : Js.Ref Bool
scheduled = Js.ref False


port : Js.Ref V
port = Js.ref Js.null


portTask : Js.Ref V
portTask = Js.ref Js.null


macrotask : V → ()
macrotask task =
    immediate = Js.global "setImmediate"
    if Js.typeIs immediate "function" then
        Js.to (Js.apply immediate [ task ])
    else
        _ =
            if Js.isNull (Js.read port) then
                channel = Js.construct (Js.global "MessageChannel") []

                _ =
                    Js.set
                        (Js.get channel "port1")
                        "onmessage"
                        (Js.from λ_ →
                            t = Js.read portTask
                            _ = Js.write portTask Js.null
                            Js.to (Js.apply t [])
                        )
                Js.write port (Js.get channel "port2")
            else
                ()
        _ = Js.write portTask task
        Js.to (Js.call (Js.read port) "postMessage" [ Js.null ])


schedule : V, V, V, V → ()
schedule task a b c =
    _ = Js.call queue "push" [ task, a, b, c ]
    if Js.read scheduled then
        ()
    else
        _ = Js.write scheduled True
        Js.to (Js.apply (Js.global "queueMicrotask") [ Js.from drain ])


resumeFiber : V, V, V → Bool
resumeFiber fiber value w =
    if not (Js.isNull w) && not (Js.same (Js.get fiber "parked") w) then
        False
    else
        _ = run fiber value
        True


enqueue : V, V, V → ()
enqueue fiber value w = schedule (Js.from resumeFiber) fiber value w


-- A fiber that throws is a defect (`boundary.md` §9.8.10 (c)): the
-- scheduler stops, the platform's hook runs, and the throw goes on to the
-- host; the teardown starts in a macrotask after it (§9.8.14). Not a
-- `catch`: nothing is caught (`CLAUDE.md` rule 9).
defect : Js.Ref V
defect = Js.ref Js.null


--| What runs when a fiber throws: a defect, after which no program code runs
--| again (`boundary.md` §9.8.10 (c)). A platform hands it what stops its
--| program — the browser stops the page — and the throw goes on to the
--| host; then every fiber is cancelled and its cleanup run, as `shutdown`
--| does (§9.8.14). The last one given is the one called.
pub onDefect : (() → ()) → ()
onDefect f = Js.write defect (Js.from f)


-- The runtime's state (`boundary.md` §9.8.14 (b)): 0 running; 1 stopping,
-- when nothing runs until the teardown starts; 2 tearing down, when only
-- fibers unwinding run; 3 stopped for good. A drain runs only at 0 and 2.
phase : Js.Ref Int
phase = Js.ref 0


-- Whether there is anything to tear down: set by the first fiber or
-- finaliser record made (`newFiber`), so a build with neither keeps none of
-- the teardown's part of a throw out of the drain, or of `shutdown`.
fibered : Js.Ref Bool
fibered = Js.ref False


-- Whether `soon` has queued work, which `shutdown` drops: so a build with
-- neither a fiber nor `soon` work keeps nothing of `shutdown` — and a
-- platform's call of it is nothing at all there.
soonQueued : Js.Ref Bool
soonQueued = Js.ref False


-- ---- Fibers ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- §6.4's record, with the continuation stack §6.4 says comes back under this
-- lowering: one literal, so one hidden class. `stack` holds continuations,
-- innermost last; `outcome` is null while it runs, then its `Exit`;
-- `observers` are called with it when it ends; `children` are what `spawn`
-- started from it, still running; `finalizers` what `bracket` and `scope`
-- registered, run last first on cancellation; `masks` how many
-- `uninterruptible` regions it is inside; `interrupted` that an interrupt
-- arrived, delivered at its next suspension point; `unwinding` that it is
-- cancelling or finishing, when interrupts are ignored; `parked` the wait it
-- is parked on; `scope` the scope that started it.
--
-- And the four slots of `transparent-effects-proposal.md` §17.5, as one
-- immutable record `{ clock, scheduler, logContext, seed }` in a field
-- `slots` that `fork` adds only once a slot has been set anywhere
-- (`slotted`), so a program that sets none pays nothing (§17.5's
-- amendment). Undefined, or a field of the record undefined, is that slot
-- at its default (`clock`: the real clock; `scheduler`: reserved, nothing
-- writes it yet). Changing a slot makes a new record, so sharing one is
-- safe.
--
-- A build that makes one — a fiber, or the record of finalisers outside any
-- — has something to tear down, and so keeps the teardown (`boundary.md`
-- §9.8.14): `fibered` is set here, so a build that makes none keeps none of
-- it.
newFiber : V, V → V
newFiber parent stack =
    _ = Js.write fibered True
    Js.from
        { children = Js.null
        , finalizers = Js.null
        , interrupted = False
        , masks = 0
        , observers = Js.null
        , outcome = Js.null
        , parent = parent
        , parked = Js.null
        , scope = Js.null
        , stack = stack
        , unwinding = False
        }


-- Queued work is dropped from now on (`runSoon`).
stopQueue : () → ()
stopQueue () = if Js.read phase == 0 then Js.write phase 1 else ()


drain : () → ()
drain () =
    if Js.bitAnd (Js.read phase) 1 ≠ 0 then
        ()
    else
        ok = Js.ref False

        emptied =
            Js.finally
                (λ() →
                    r = drainFrom 0
                    _ = Js.write ok True
                    r
                )
                λ() → if Js.read ok then () else guard ()
        if emptied then
            _ = Js.set queue "length" (Js.from 0)
            _ = Js.write head 0
            Js.write scheduled False
        else
            ()


-- The drain saw a throw, which goes on to the host once its cleanup ends.
guard : () → ()
guard () =
    if Js.read fibered then
        failed ()
    else
        _ = Js.write phase 1
        d = Js.read defect
        if Js.isNull d then () else Js.to (Js.apply d [ Js.null ])


-- Run ready work until the queue is empty (`True`), or until 64
-- resumptions have run or the work just run stopped the runtime, when the
-- rest continues in a macrotask (`False`), so a page renders and its timers
-- fire (research/16 §5.5).
drainFrom : Int → Bool
drainFrom count =
    h = Js.read head
    if h ≥ Js.to (Js.get queue "length") then
        True
    else if count == 64 || Js.read phase == 1 then
        _ = macrotask (Js.from drain)
        False
    else
        task = Js.at queue h
        a = Js.at queue (h + 1)
        b = Js.at queue (h + 2)
        c = Js.at queue (h + 3)
        _ = Js.setAt queue h Js.null
        _ = Js.setAt queue (h + 1) Js.null
        _ = Js.setAt queue (h + 2) Js.null
        _ = Js.setAt queue (h + 3) Js.null
        _ = Js.write head (h + 4)
        drainFrom (if Js.to (Js.apply task [ a, b, c ]) then count + 1 else count)


--| Stop every fiber: close every root scope, cancel every fiber and run its
--| cleanup, drop queued work, and start nothing new. Cleanup that suspends
--| is given `deadline` milliseconds from the call; `done` is called once
--| every fiber has ended, with how many cleanups were cut short. What a
--| platform calls when its program stops (`boundary.md` §9.8.14); a
--| program never does. It returns at once — the cleanup runs in a later
--| task — and a second call does nothing.
pub shutdown : Int, sync (Int → ()) → ()
shutdown ms over =
    _ = if Js.read soonQueued then stopQueue () else ()
    if Js.read fibered then closeAll ms (Js.from over) else ()


-- The drain's guard saw a throw, which goes on to the host once this
-- returns. The state the throw left behind is reset first. The first one
-- is the defect: the runtime stops and the teardown is scheduled, the
-- fiber that threw (the culprit) noted for it, and the platform's hook
-- stops the page. One while tearing down is a cleanup's (§9.8.14 (g)): the
-- fiber goes on to its next finaliser, the drain in a new macrotask.
failed : () → ()
failed () =
    fiber = Js.read current
    _ = Js.write current Js.null
    _ = Js.write pending Js.null
    _ = Js.write soonRunning Js.null
    o = Js.read outside
    _ = if Js.isNull o then () else Js.set o "masks" (Js.from 0)

    -- A throw that stopped the page on its way here — an `update` a body's
    -- send ran — has already made the runtime stop: it is still the defect.
    if Js.read phase < 2 then
        _ = Js.write culprit fiber
        _ = stopping ()
        d = Js.read defect
        if Js.isNull d then () else Js.to (Js.apply d [ Js.null ])
    else
        _ =
            if not (Js.isNull fiber) && Js.isNull (Js.get fiber "outcome") then
                _ = recover fiber
                enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
            else
                ()
        macrotask (Js.from drain)


-- ---- The run loop ----------------------------------------------------------

run : V, V → ()
run fiber first =
    outer = Js.read current
    _ = Js.write current fiber
    _ = Js.set fiber "parked" Js.null
    _ = loop fiber first
    Js.write current outer


loop : V, V → ()
loop fiber first =
    value =
        if deliverable fiber then
            _ = unwind fiber
            Js.null
        else
            first
    next = Js.call (Js.get fiber "stack") "pop" []
    result = Js.apply next [ value ]
    if not (Js.isNull (Js.get fiber "outcome")) then
        ()
    else if Js.same result sentinel then
        p = Js.read pending
        _ = Js.write pending Js.null
        ks = Js.get p "ks"
        _ = pushBack (Js.get fiber "stack") ks (Js.to (Js.get ks "length") - 1)
        if Js.to (Js.get p "interrupt") then
            -- Cancelled by itself (a joined fiber that was cancelled), or
            -- an interrupt delivered at this suspension point: unwind now,
            -- whatever the masks say, since there is no value to go on with.
            _ = unwind fiber
            loop fiber Js.null
        else if Js.read finalising && Js.read expired && inCleanup fiber then
            -- Past the teardown's deadline a finaliser runs only to its
            -- first wait, and the fiber goes on to its next (§9.8.14 (f)).
            _ = abandon fiber (Js.get p "wait")
            loop fiber Js.null
        else
            Js.set fiber "parked" (Js.get p "wait")
    else
        loop fiber result


pushBack : V, V, Int → ()
pushBack stack ks i =
    if i < 0 then
        ()
    else
        _ = Js.call stack "push" [ Js.at ks i ]
        pushBack stack ks (i - 1)


-- Park the current fiber until `register`'s resume is called, or answer at
-- once when it is called before `register` returns: `done` then. `register` returns a
-- canceller, or null.
suspend : sync (V → V) → a
suspend register =
    fiber = Js.read current
    if deliverable fiber then
        park Js.null True
    else
        w = Js.from { cancel = Js.null, done = False, ready = False, sync = True, value = Js.null }

        wake =
            λvalue →
                if Js.to (Js.get w "done") then
                    ()
                else
                    _ = Js.set w "done" (Js.from True)
                    if Js.to (Js.get w "sync") then
                        _ = Js.set w "ready" (Js.from True)
                        Js.set w "value" value
                    else
                        enqueue fiber value w
        canceller = register (Js.from wake)
        _ = Js.set w "sync" (Js.from False)
        if Js.to (Js.get w "ready") then
            Js.to (Js.get w "value")
        else
            _ = Js.set w "cancel" canceller
            park w False


-- The current fiber cancels itself: there is no value to return.
selfCancel : () → a
selfCancel () =
    _ = Js.set (Js.read current) "interrupted" (Js.from True)
    park Js.null True


-- ---- Ending, and interruption (§6.2) ---------------------------------------

complete : V, V → ()
complete fiber outcome =
    _ = Js.set fiber "outcome" outcome
    _ = Js.set fiber "stack" Js.null
    _ = Js.write live (Js.read live - 1)
    sc = Js.get fiber "scope"

    _ =
        if not (Js.isNull sc) then
            Js.to (Js.call (Js.get sc "children") "delete" [ fiber ])
        else if Js.read spawning && not (Js.isNull (Js.get fiber "parent")) then
            parent = Js.get fiber "parent"
            if Js.isNull (Js.get parent "children") then
                ()
            else
                Js.to (Js.call (Js.get parent "children") "delete" [ fiber ])
        else
            unlist fiber
    observers = Js.get fiber "observers"
    _ = Js.set fiber "observers" Js.null
    _ = if Js.isNull observers then () else Js.each observers λo → Js.to (Js.apply o [ fiber ])
    if Js.read live == 0 && Js.read phase == 2 then allEnded () else ()


observe : V, V → ()
observe fiber observer =
    if Js.isNull (Js.get fiber "observers") then
        Js.set fiber "observers" (Js.array [ observer ])
    else
        Js.to (Js.call (Js.get fiber "observers") "push" [ observer ])


unobserve : V, V → ()
unobserve fiber observer =
    os = Js.get fiber "observers"
    if Js.isNull os then
        ()
    else
        i : Int
        i = Js.to (Js.call os "indexOf" [ observer ])
        if i ≥ 0 then Js.to (Js.call os "splice" [ Js.from i, Js.from 1 ]) else ()


-- Interrupt `fiber`: resume it at once if it is parked where it may be
-- interrupted — its wait's canceller runs and the wait's later answer is
-- dropped — or latch the interrupt for its next suspension point.
halt : V → ()
halt fiber =
    if not (Js.isNull (Js.get fiber "outcome")) || Js.to (Js.get fiber "unwinding") then
        ()
    else
        _ = Js.set fiber "interrupted" (Js.from True)
        w = Js.get fiber "parked"
        if Js.isNull w || Js.to (Js.get fiber "masks") ≠ 0 then
            ()
        else
            _ = Js.set fiber "parked" Js.null
            _ = Js.set w "done" (Js.from True)

            -- Queued before its canceller runs, so a canceller that throws
            -- cannot leave a fiber that never unwinds (§9.8.14 (d) step 1).
            _ = enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
            canceller = Js.get w "cancel"
            if Js.isNull canceller then () else Js.to (Js.apply canceller [ Js.null ])


-- Park until every one of `fibers` has ended; at once when they have.
waitAll : V → ()
waitAll fibers =
    left = Js.ref 0
    _ = Js.each fibers λf →
        if Js.isNull (Js.get f "outcome") then Js.write left (Js.read left + 1) else ()
    if Js.read left == 0 then
        ()
    else
        suspend λwake →
            each = Js.from λ_ →
                _ = Js.write left (Js.read left - 1)
                if Js.read left == 0 then Js.to (Js.apply wake [ Js.null ]) else ()
            _ = Js.each fibers λf → if Js.isNull (Js.get f "outcome") then observe f each else ()
            Js.from λ_ → Js.each fibers λf → unobserve f each


-- Interrupt `fibers` and wait for them.
cancelEvery : V → ()
cancelEvery fibers =
    _ = Js.each fibers λf → halt f
    waitAll fibers


-- The bottom of every fiber's stack: its children are cancelled and waited
-- for, then it is done.
finish : V → V
finish value =
    fiber = Js.read current
    _ = Js.set fiber "unwinding" (Js.from True)
    if not (Js.read spawning) then
        finished value
    else
        children = Js.get fiber "children"
        if none children then
            finished value
        else
            _ = cancelEvery (copy children)
            finished value


finished : V → V
finished value =
    _ = complete (Js.read current) (host (Done value))
    value


-- Replace `fiber`'s stack with its cancellation: its children first, then
-- its finalisers, last first, then its end (§16.4, the owner's A11). Each
-- finaliser runs above a boundary, so a teardown can cut what it left on
-- the stack back to the next one (`boundary.md` §9.8.14 (d) step 3); the
-- fibers inside one are `cleaning`.
unwind : V → ()
unwind fiber =
    _ = Js.set fiber "unwinding" (Js.from True)
    _ = Js.set fiber "parked" Js.null
    stack = Js.get fiber "stack"
    _ = Js.set stack "length" (Js.from 0)
    _ = Js.call stack "push" [ Js.from ended ]
    _ = if Js.read finalising then cleanups fiber else ()
    if Js.read spawning then Js.to (Js.call stack "push" [ Js.from stopChildren ]) else ()


-- Move `fiber`'s finalisers onto its stack, each above a boundary, to run
-- last first.
cleanups : V → ()
cleanups fiber =
    fins = Js.get fiber "finalizers"
    _ = Js.set fiber "finalizers" Js.null
    stack = Js.get fiber "stack"
    if Js.isNull fins then
        ()
    else
        Js.each fins λfin →
            Js.to
                (Js.call stack "push"
                    [ Js.from boundary
                    , Js.from λ_ →
                        _ = Js.call (cleaningSet ()) "add" [ Js.read current ]
                        Js.apply fin [ Js.null ]
                    ]
                )


-- The fibers inside a finaliser; made on first use.
cleaning : Js.Ref V
cleaning = Js.ref Js.null


cleaningSet : () → V
cleaningSet () =
    c = Js.read cleaning
    if Js.isNull c then
        s = Js.construct (Js.global "Set") []
        _ = Js.write cleaning s
        s
    else
        c


inCleanup : V → Bool
inCleanup fiber =
    c = Js.read cleaning
    not (Js.isNull c) && Js.to (Js.call c "has" [ fiber ])


boundary : V → V
boundary value =
    _ = Js.call (Js.read cleaning) "delete" [ Js.read current ]
    value


-- Discard what the finaliser `fiber` is inside left on its stack: it goes
-- on to its next finaliser, the one it was in counting as run. What that
-- one opened and had not yet closed — a `bracket`, a `scope` — is released
-- first, as it would have been had its use been interrupted.
cutBack : V → ()
cutBack fiber =
    _ = popTo (Js.get fiber "stack")
    _ = Js.call (Js.read cleaning) "delete" [ fiber ]
    cleanups fiber


popTo : V → ()
popTo stack =
    if Js.to (Js.get stack "length") == 0 then
        ()
    else if Js.same (Js.call stack "pop" []) (Js.from boundary) then
        ()
    else
        popTo stack


stopChildren : V → ()
stopChildren _ =
    children = Js.get (Js.read current) "children"
    if none children then () else cancelEvery (copy children)


ended : V → ()
ended _ = complete (Js.read current) cancelled


-- `ended` for a fiber whose finalisers started children (`spawn`): those
-- are cancelled and waited for first, so that nothing a fiber starts
-- outlives it; looked at again after the wait.
reap : V → ()
reap _ =
    children = Js.get (Js.read current) "children"
    if none children then
        ended Js.null
    else
        _ = cancelEvery (copy children)
        reap Js.null


-- ---- The API ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- `from` is what the new fiber copies its slots from (`slotsOf`).
fork : V, V, V, V → V
fork parent work sc from =
    -- `work` is the stack's first continuation as it is: the run loop calls
    -- it with the value the fiber starts with, null, which a function of
    -- `()` takes as its argument.
    fiber = newFiber parent (Js.array [ Js.from finish, work ])
    _ = if Js.read slotted then Js.set fiber "slots" (slotsOf from) else ()
    _ = Js.write live (Js.read live + 1)

    _ =
        if not (Js.isNull sc) then
            _ = Js.set fiber "scope" sc

            _ =
                if Js.to (Js.get sc "closed") then
                    Js.set fiber "interrupted" (Js.from True)
                else if Js.isNull (Js.get sc "finalizer") then
                    -- A root is listed when it is first given a fiber, so
                    -- that a build which opens one and starts none keeps no
                    -- registry (§9.8.14 (c)). A nested scope's finaliser is
                    -- its close; a root's is null until it is listed, and
                    -- `false` after.
                    _ = Js.set sc "finalizer" (Js.from False)
                    Js.to (Js.call roots "push" [ sc ])
                else
                    ()
            Js.to (Js.call (Js.get sc "children") "add" [ fiber ])
        else if Js.read spawning && not (Js.isNull parent) then
            _ =
                if Js.isNull (Js.get parent "children") then
                    Js.set parent "children" (Js.construct (Js.global "Set") [])
                else
                    ()
            Js.to (Js.call (Js.get parent "children") "add" [ fiber ])
        else
            Js.to (Js.call roots "push" [ fiber ])

    -- Started while the runtime stops: cancelled before it runs.
    _ = if Js.read phase ≠ 0 then Js.set fiber "interrupted" (Js.from True) else ()
    _ = enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
    fiber


--| Wait for a platform's callback: the one way a fiber suspends. The
--| function is called at once with the `Resume` the platform hands its host
--| callback, and returns what cancels the wait. When the host calls back
--| before the function returns, nothing waits at all.
--|
--|     sleep ms =
--|         Task.callback λresume → startTimer ms resume
pub callback : sync (Resume a → (() → ())) → a
callback register = suspend λwake →
    canceller = Js.from (register (Js.to wake))
    if Js.typeIs canceller "function" then canceller else Js.null


-- Work outside any fiber, `{ end, kids, w }`, while it runs.
soonRunning : Js.Ref V
soonRunning = Js.ref Js.null


-- Outside any fiber but inside work `soon` runs, a child belongs to that
-- work and is cancelled when it returns — where a fiber's `finish` would
-- have cancelled it (`boundary.md` §9.8.11 (b)). It cannot have run yet: it
-- is queued behind the work.
endSoon : V → ()
endSoon s = Js.each (Js.get s "kids") λf → halt f


--| Start `work` in a new fiber, a child of the current one, and return at
--| once. The child is cancelled when the current fiber ends.
pub spawn : (() → a) → Fiber a
spawn work =
    _ = Js.write spawning True
    parent = Js.read current
    s = Js.read soonRunning
    if not (Js.isNull parent) then
        child = fork parent (Js.from work) Js.null parent

        -- Started by a finaliser of a fiber that is unwinding — after
        -- `stopChildren` cancelled its children (A11) — so its end, at the
        -- bottom of its stack, cancels and waits for this one too. Effect
        -- likewise interrupts a fiber's children once its whole stack has
        -- unwound.
        _ =
            if Js.to (Js.get parent "unwinding") then
                Js.setAt (Js.get parent "stack") 0 (Js.from reap)
            else
                ()
        Js.to child
    else if Js.isNull s then
        Js.to (fork Js.null (Js.from work) Js.null Js.null)
    else
        child = fork Js.null (Js.from work) Js.null Js.null
        _ = if Js.isNullish (Js.get s "kids") then Js.set s "kids" (Js.array []) else ()
        _ = Js.call (Js.get s "kids") "push" [ child ]
        _ = Js.set s "end" (Js.from endSoon)
        Js.to child


--| Start `work` in a new fiber that belongs to `scope`.
pub spawnIn : Scope, (() → a) → Fiber a
spawnIn sc work = Js.to (fork (Js.read current) (Js.from work) (Js.from sc) (Js.read current))


--| Whether stopping will have cleanup to run: `True` once a fiber has been
--| made, when `shutdown` cancels fibers and calls its `done`. What a
--| platform asks to know whether more reports may follow its program's
--| stop (`boundary.md` §9.8.14 (g)).
pub cleansUp : () → Bool
cleansUp () = Js.read fibered


--| Run `work` in a root fiber, and call `done` with how it ended. What a
--| platform's entry point uses; a program asks its platform instead.
pub start : (() → a), sync (Exit a → ()) → ()
start work report =
    fiber = fork Js.null (Js.from work) Js.null Js.undefined
    observe fiber (Js.from λf → report (guest (Js.get f "outcome")))


joined : Exit a → a
joined outcome =
    case outcome of
        Done a →
            a

        Cancelled →
            selfCancel ()


outcomeOf : V → Exit a
outcomeOf fiber = suspend λwake →
    o = Js.from λf → Js.apply wake [ Js.get f "outcome" ]
    _ = observe fiber o
    Js.from λ_ → unobserve fiber o


--| Wait for a fiber's value. If it was cancelled, the fiber that joins it is
--| cancelled too.
pub join : Fiber a → a
join fiber =
    f = Js.from fiber
    if Js.isNull (Js.get f "outcome") then
        -- The protocol by hand, as `Task.js` wrote it: the wait is called
        -- as data, and when it parks `joined` itself goes on the stack, so
        -- a join that waits makes no continuation of its own — the
        -- lowering's would be a closure per join (`joined` may suspend, so
        -- it cannot go to `andThen`, whose argument is `sync`).
        r = Js.apply (Js.from outcomeOf) [ f ]
        Js.suspending λ() →
            if Js.same r sentinel then
                _ = Js.call (Js.get (Js.read pending) "ks") "push" [ Js.from joined ]
                Js.to sentinel
            else
                Js.to (Js.apply (Js.from joined) [ r ])
    else
        joined (guest (Js.get f "outcome"))


--| Wait for a fiber to end, and say how.
pub wait : Fiber a → Exit a
wait fiber =
    f = Js.from fiber
    if Js.isNull (Js.get f "outcome") then
        outcomeOf f
    else
        guest (Js.get f "outcome")


--| Cancel a fiber and wait until its cleanup has run. Cancelling a fiber
--| that has ended does nothing.
pub cancel : Fiber a → ()
cancel fiber =
    f = Js.from fiber
    if Js.same f (Js.read current) then
        selfCancel ()
    else if not (Js.isNull (Js.get f "outcome")) then
        ()
    else
        _ = halt f
        waitAll (Js.array [ f ])


--| Let every other fiber that is ready run first.
pub yieldNow : () → ()
yieldNow () =
    fiber = Js.read current
    if deliverable fiber then
        selfCancel ()
    else
        w = Js.from { cancel = Js.null, done = False, ready = False, sync = False, value = Js.null }
        _ = enqueue fiber Js.null w
        park w False


--| Answer the wait `resume` belongs to with `value`: the fiber that waits
--| is queued to go on with it, and runs at a later turn, never inside this
--| call. Once only: a second `resume` of the same wait does nothing, and so
--| does one after the waiting fiber was cancelled. Called while the
--| function `callback` was given is still running, it answers the wait at
--| once and nothing waits at all.
--|
--| What lets a program finish a wait it started itself, and so write its
--| own coordination — a gate, a mailbox — over `callback` and a `Ref`.
--|
--|     gate = Ref.make Nothing
--|     opened = Task.spawn λ() → Task.callback λr →
--|         _ = Ref.set gate (Just r)
--|         λ() → Ref.set gate Nothing
--|     -- later, from another fiber:
--|     case Ref.get gate of
--|         Just r → Task.resume r "open"
--|         Nothing → ()
pub resume : Resume a, a → ()
resume r value = Js.to (Js.apply (Js.from r) [ Js.from value ])


--| Wait forever. Only cancelling the fiber ends the wait. Effect's `never`.
pub never : () → a
never () = callback λ_ → λ() → ()


--| How a fiber ended, `Just` once it has and `Nothing` while it runs,
--| without waiting. A fiber that is cancelled but still running its cleanup
--| is running.
pub poll : Fiber a → Maybe (Exit a)
poll fiber =
    o = Js.get (Js.from fiber) "outcome"
    if Js.isNull o then Nothing else Just (guest o)


-- The fibers of a list, as an array to wait on.
fiberArray : List (Fiber a) → V
fiberArray fibers = List.foldl fibers (Js.array []) λf arr →
    _ = Js.call arr "push" [ Js.from f ]
    arr


-- The values of fibers that have all ended: `Nothing` when one was
-- cancelled.
values : List (Fiber a) → Maybe (List a)
values fibers = List.foldr fibers (Just []) λf acc →
    case acc of
        Just rest →
            case guest (Js.get (Js.from f) "outcome") of
                Done v →
                    Just [ v, …rest ]

                Cancelled →
                    Nothing

        Nothing →
            Nothing


--| Wait for every fiber in the list, then answer their values, in list
--| order. If any of them was cancelled, the fiber that waits is cancelled
--| too, as `join` of that one would — but only once every fiber has ended.
--| A fiber named twice is waited for once and its value given twice.
pub joinAll : List (Fiber a) → List a
joinAll fibers =
    _ = waitAll (fiberArray fibers)

    case values fibers of
        Just vs →
            vs

        Nothing →
            selfCancel ()


--| Cancel every fiber in the list, in list order, and wait until all of
--| them have ended and run their cleanup. A fiber that has ended is left
--| as it is; a fiber that belongs to a scope still belongs to it.
pub cancelAll : List (Fiber a) → ()
cancelAll fibers = cancelEvery (fiberArray fibers)


--| Start `work` in a new fiber that belongs to no other: it outlives the
--| fiber that started it, and is not cancelled when that one ends. What
--| ends it is its own end, `cancel`, or the program's: a page's stop, or on
--| Node the end of `Io.run`'s fiber, cancels it and runs its cleanup with
--| every other fiber's. It sees what the fiber that started it sees — its
--| clock, its log context. Effect's `forkDetach`.
pub spawnDetached : (() → a) → Fiber a
spawnDetached work = Js.to (fork Js.null (Js.from work) Js.null (Js.read current))


openScope : () → Scope
openScope () =
    sc =
        Js.from
            { children = Js.construct (Js.global "Set") [], closed = False, finalizer = Js.null }
    _ = Js.set sc "finalizer" (Js.from λ_ → shutAll sc)
    _ = addFinalizer (here ()) (Js.get sc "finalizer")
    Js.to sc


-- Whether a finaliser has ever been registered (here, or by the fiber
-- `cleanupFiber` starts): until one has, no fiber holds one, and none can be
-- inside one when the teardown's deadline passes. A build that registers
-- none — a page whose fibers only wait — folds this to `False` and keeps
-- none of the finaliser walk or its boundaries.
finalising : Js.Ref Bool
finalising = Js.ref False


-- Put `fin` on `fiber`'s finalisers, last.
addFinalizer : V, V → ()
addFinalizer fiber fin =
    _ = Js.write finalising True
    fins = Js.get fiber "finalizers"

    if Js.isNull fins then
        Js.set fiber "finalizers" (Js.array [ fin ])
    else
        Js.to (Js.call fins "push" [ fin ])


dropFinalizer : V, V → ()
dropFinalizer fiber fin =
    fins = Js.get fiber "finalizers"
    if Js.isNull fins then
        ()
    else
        i : Int
        i = Js.to (Js.call fins "lastIndexOf" [ fin ])
        if i ≥ 0 then Js.to (Js.call fins "splice" [ Js.from i, Js.from 1 ]) else ()


-- Close `sc`: a fiber started in it from now on — by the release of one
-- being cancelled — is cancelled before it runs, as in a closed root, and
-- every fiber in it is cancelled and waited for, again until none is left.
shut : V → ()
shut sc =
    _ = Js.set sc "closed" (Js.from True)
    children = Js.get sc "children"
    if Js.to (Js.get children "size") == 0 then
        ()
    else
        _ = cancelEvery (copy children)
        shut sc


closeScope : Scope, a → a
closeScope sc value =
    fiber = here ()
    s = Js.from sc

    -- The scope's fibers have all ended, as they mostly have: closed at
    -- once, so the call that may suspend — and the continuation the
    -- lowering makes for it — is only on the slow path.
    if Js.to (Js.get (Js.get s "children") "size") == 0 then
        _ = Js.set s "closed" (Js.from True)
        _ = dropFinalizer fiber (Js.get s "finalizer")
        if Js.read deferring then afterDeferred s (host (Done ())) value else value
    else
        _ = shut s
        _ = dropFinalizer fiber (Js.get s "finalizer")
        if Js.read deferring then afterDeferred s (host (Done ())) value else value


-- ---- Deferred finalisers (§17.3, `defer`) -----------------------------------

-- Whether `defer` has run: a scope's deferred finalisers are looked for only
-- then, so a build that never defers keeps none of this.
deferring : Js.Ref Bool
deferring = Js.ref False


-- What runs them, `{ roots, run }`, set by `defer`: the scope code above
-- reaches it only through this cell, so what it needs is kept — and placed
-- in the output — only in a build that defers.
deferral : Js.Ref V
deferral = Js.ref Js.null


-- Run the deferred finalisers of `s`, told `exit`, then answer `value`:
-- `deferral`'s `run`, with the protocol by hand, as `join` writes it.
afterDeferred : V, V, a → a
afterDeferred s exit value =
    r = Js.apply (Js.get (Js.read deferral) "run") [ s, exit ]

    Js.suspending λ() →
        if Js.same r sentinel then
            _ = Js.call (Js.get (Js.read pending) "ks") "push" [ Js.from λ_ → Js.from value ]
            Js.to sentinel
        else
            value


-- A scope's finaliser on its fiber's list: run when that fiber is cancelled
-- inside the scope's function, so the deferred finalisers are told
-- `Cancelled`.
shutAll : V → ()
shutAll sc = if Js.read deferring then shutWith sc cancelled else shut sc


-- Close `sc`, then run its deferred finalisers, told `exit`.
shutWith : V, V → ()
shutWith sc exit =
    _ = shut sc
    afterDeferred sc exit ()


-- Run the deferred finalisers of the scope `s`, last added first, where
-- cancellation cannot reach them, each told `exit`. Taken off the scope
-- first, so that they run once.
runDeferred : V, V → ()
runDeferred s exit =
    d = Js.get s "deferred"

    if Js.isNullish d then
        ()
    else
        _ = Js.set s "deferred" Js.null
        uninterruptible λ() → runEach d exit


-- Call the functions in `fins`, last first, with `exit`, each one ended
-- before the next starts. The protocol by hand, as `join` writes it: a
-- function that parks has the rest of the list pushed after it.
runEach : V, V → ()
runEach fins exit =
    if Js.to (Js.get fins "length") == 0 then
        ()
    else
        r = Js.apply (Js.call fins "pop" []) [ exit ]

        Js.suspending λ() →
            if Js.same r sentinel then
                _ =
                    Js.call (Js.get (Js.read pending) "ks") "push"
                        [ Js.from λ_ → Js.apply (Js.from runEach) [ fins, exit ] ]
                Js.to sentinel
            else
                Js.to (Js.apply (Js.from runEach) [ fins, exit ])


-- A fiber of its own for finalisers that belong to no running fiber: it
-- runs `fins`, last first, where nothing can interrupt them, and ends. The
-- teardown waits for it, as for every fiber.
cleanupFiber : V → ()
cleanupFiber fins =
    fiber = newFiber Js.null (Js.array [])
    _ = Js.write live (Js.read live + 1)
    _ = Js.write finalising True
    _ = Js.set fiber "finalizers" fins
    _ = unwind fiber
    enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null


--| Run `finally` when `scope` closes — after every fiber started in it has
--| been cancelled and has ended — where cancellation cannot reach it, the
--| last one added first. It is told `Done ()` when the scope's function
--| returned, and `Cancelled` when the fiber running that function was
--| cancelled. Added to a scope that has already closed, it runs at once,
--| told `Cancelled`. Effect's `Scope.addFinalizer`.
--|
--|     Task.scope λs →
--|         conn = connect ()
--|         _ = Task.defer s λ_ → disconnect conn
--|         serve s conn
--|
--| A root scope's run when `closeRoot` closes it, told `Done ()`, in a
--| fiber of their own that `closeRoot` does not wait for; or when the
--| program stops, told `Cancelled`, with the rest of its cleanup.
pub defer : Scope, (Exit () → ()) → ()
defer sc cleanup =
    s = Js.from sc

    if Js.to (Js.get s "closed") then
        uninterruptible λ() → cleanup Cancelled
    else
        _ = Js.write deferring True
        _ = Js.write deferral (Js.from { roots = Js.from deferRoots, run = Js.from runDeferred })
        _ = Js.write fibered True

        _ =
            if Js.isNullish (Js.get s "deferred") then
                Js.set s "deferred" (Js.array [])
            else
                ()

        -- A root that has run no fiber is listed now, so that the program's
        -- stop finds it (`fork`).
        _ =
            if Js.isNull (Js.get s "finalizer") then
                _ = Js.set s "finalizer" (Js.from False)
                Js.to (Js.call roots "push" [ s ])
            else
                ()
        Js.to (Js.call (Js.get s "deferred") "push" [ Js.from cleanup ])


--| Whether a fiber is still running: `False` once it has ended, either
--| way. A fiber that has been cancelled but is still running its cleanup
--| is still running.
pub running : Fiber a → Bool
running fiber = Js.isNull (Js.get (Js.from fiber) "outcome")


-- Work run in no fiber, where a fiber started now would first run
-- (`boundary.md` §9.8.11): `{ end, kids, w }`, the work until it runs. Work
-- that runs owns what it `spawn`s, as a fiber does its children: they are
-- cancelled when it returns (`spawn`), so a body keeps the structure a fiber
-- gave it. No fiber is made: the record is the work's own, and `end` is set
-- only by a `spawn`, so a build that never spawns keeps nothing of
-- cancellation here.
runSoon : V → Bool
runSoon s =
    w = Js.get s "w"
    _ = Js.set s "w" Js.null

    -- Program code, which no longer runs once the runtime stops: dropped.
    if Js.read phase ≠ 0 then
        False
    else
        outer = Js.read soonRunning
        _ = Js.write soonRunning s
        _ = Js.apply w [ Js.null ]
        _ = Js.write soonRunning outer

        -- Only a `spawn` sets `end`, and the work may have been the first
        -- to spawn: `spawning` is read after it.
        _ =
            if Js.read spawning then
                end = Js.get s "end"
                if Js.isNullish end then () else Js.to (Js.apply end [ s ])
            else
                ()
        True


--| Queue `work` to run at the scheduler's next turn, in the queue of the
--| fibers that are ready, behind those queued before it — exactly where a
--| fiber `spawn`ed now would first run — but with no fiber of its own:
--| `work` must not suspend, and it runs outside any fiber, as `main` does.
--| What a page program runs a command with when its body cannot suspend
--| (`boundary.md` §9.8.11). What `work` starts with `spawn` belongs to it,
--| as a fiber's children do, and is cancelled when it returns. Nothing stops it: a fiber that has not started
--| runs until it first suspends before anything can cancel it, and work
--| that never suspends runs to its end.
pub soon : sync (() → ()) → Soon
soon work =
    _ = Js.write soonQueued True
    s = Js.from { w = Js.from work }
    _ = schedule (Js.from runSoon) s Js.null Js.null
    Js.to s


--| Whether queued work has not run yet.
pub queued : Soon → Bool
queued s = not (Js.isNull (Js.get (Js.from s) "w"))


--| A scope that no function brackets, for a platform whose program
--| outlives every call: a page program's commands and subscriptions run
--| in one. `closeRoot` ends it; nothing else does.
pub openRoot : () → Scope
openRoot () =
    Js.to
        (Js.from
            { children = Js.construct (Js.global "Set") [], closed = False, finalizer = Js.null }
        )


--| Cancel every fiber of a scope `openRoot` made, without waiting for
--| their cleanup, which runs as each is resumed. A fiber started in the
--| scope afterwards is cancelled before it runs. What `defer` added to it
--| runs once those fibers have ended, in a fiber of its own.
pub closeRoot : Scope → ()
closeRoot sc =
    s = Js.from sc
    _ = unlist s
    _ = Js.set s "closed" (Js.from True)
    _ = Js.each (copy (Js.get s "children")) λf → halt f

    if Js.read deferring then
        Js.to (Js.apply (Js.get (Js.read deferral) "roots") [ Js.array [ s ], host (Done ()) ])
    else
        ()


-- ---- Shutdown (`boundary.md` §9.8.14) --------------------------------------

-- Every root, in the order it first ran a fiber: each scope `openRoot` made
-- that has been given one and that `closeRoot` has not closed, and each
-- fiber with neither a parent nor a scope — `start`'s, and `spawn`'s
-- outside any fiber — that has not ended.
roots : V
roots = Js.array []


unlist : V → ()
unlist root =
    i : Int
    i = Js.to (Js.call roots "indexOf" [ root ])
    if i ≥ 0 then Js.to (Js.call roots "splice" [ Js.from i, Js.from 1 ]) else ()


-- The fibers that have not ended, so the teardown knows when it is over.
live : Js.Ref Int
live = Js.ref 0


-- The teardown's: the fiber whose throw was the defect, the deadline and
-- `done` `shutdown` was given, its timer, whether it has passed, how many
-- finalisers it cut short, the fibers the sweep has still to reach, and
-- whether the teardown is scheduled.
culprit : Js.Ref V
culprit = Js.ref Js.null


deadline : Js.Ref Int
deadline = Js.ref (-1)


whenDone : Js.Ref V
whenDone = Js.ref Js.null


deadlineTimer : Js.Ref V
deadlineTimer = Js.ref Js.null


expired : Js.Ref Bool
expired = Js.ref False


abandoned : Js.Ref Int
abandoned = Js.ref 0


sweeping : V
sweeping = Js.array []


swept : Js.Ref Int
swept = Js.ref 0


torn : Js.Ref Bool
torn = Js.ref False


-- Stop, and schedule the teardown once.
stopping : () → ()
stopping () =
    _ = if Js.read phase == 0 then Js.write phase 1 else ()
    _ = Js.write scheduled True
    if Js.read torn then
        ()
    else
        _ = Js.write torn True
        macrotask (Js.from teardown)


-- `shutdown`'s part here: the first call's deadline and `done`; a second
-- call does nothing.
closeAll : Int, V → ()
closeAll ms over =
    if not (Js.isNull (Js.read whenDone)) || Js.read phase == 3 then
        ()
    else
        _ = Js.write whenDone over
        _ = Js.write deadline ms
        _ = if Js.read phase == 2 then arm () else ()
        stopping ()


arm : () → ()
arm () =
    Js.write deadlineTimer
        (Js.apply (Js.global "setTimeout") [ Js.from expire, Js.from (Js.read deadline) ])


-- The sweep (§9.8.14 (d) step 1): every root scope closed and every fiber
-- of every root interrupted, in the order they were listed — each parked
-- fiber's canceller runs now, so what the host holds is released before any
-- finaliser runs — then the culprit unwound, and a fiber started for the
-- finalisers a throw left outside any fiber. A canceller that throws is
-- reported by the host; the sweep goes on at the next fiber, in a new
-- macrotask. Then the drain unwinds them all.
teardown : () → ()
teardown () =
    _ =
        if Js.read phase == 1 then
            _ = Js.write phase 2
            _ = if Js.isNull (Js.read whenDone) then () else arm ()
            _ = Js.each roots λroot →
                if Js.isUndefined (Js.get root "stack") then
                    _ = Js.set root "closed" (Js.from True)
                    Js.each (Js.get root "children") λf → Js.to (Js.call sweeping "push" [ f ])
                else
                    Js.to (Js.call sweeping "push" [ root ])
            if Js.read deferring then
                Js.to (Js.apply (Js.get (Js.read deferral) "roots") [ roots, cancelled ])
            else
                ()
        else
            ()
    ok = Js.ref False

    _ =
        Js.finally
            (λ() →
                _ = sweep ()
                Js.write ok True
            )
            λ() → if Js.read ok then () else macrotask (Js.from teardown)
    c = Js.read culprit

    _ =
        if Js.isNull c then
            ()
        else
            _ = Js.write culprit Js.null
            if Js.isNull (Js.get c "outcome") then
                _ = recover c
                enqueue c Js.null Js.null
            else
                ()
    o = Js.read outside

    _ =
        if not (Js.read finalising) || Js.isNull o || none (Js.get o "finalizers") then
            ()
        else
            fiber = newFiber Js.null (Js.array [])
            _ = Js.write live (Js.read live + 1)
            _ = Js.set fiber "finalizers" (Js.get o "finalizers")
            _ = Js.set o "finalizers" Js.null
            _ = Js.set o "masks" (Js.from 0)
            _ = unwind fiber
            enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
    if Js.read live == 0 then allEnded () else drain ()


-- The deferred finalisers of the root scopes among `list`: each root's run
-- once its fibers have ended, told `exit`, in one fiber started for them
-- all, as the finalisers outside any fiber are — the roots in list order,
-- so each goes in front of those before it. What `closeRoot` (with its one
-- root, told `Done ()`) and the program's stop (with every root, told
-- `Cancelled`) call, through `deferral`.
deferRoots : V, V → ()
deferRoots list exit =
    fins = Js.array []

    _ = Js.each list λroot →
        if Js.isUndefined (Js.get root "stack") && not (Js.isNullish (Js.get root "deferred")) then
            Js.to (Js.call fins "unshift" [ Js.from λ_ → shutWith root exit ])
        else
            ()
    if Js.to (Js.get fins "length") == 0 then () else cleanupFiber fins


sweep : () → ()
sweep () =
    i = Js.read swept
    if i < Js.to (Js.get sweeping "length") then
        _ = Js.write swept (i + 1)
        _ = halt (Js.at sweeping i)
        sweep ()
    else
        ()


-- Put a fiber whose code threw back on the road to its end: out of the
-- finaliser it was in, to the next; or, if it was not unwinding, unwound.
recover : V → ()
recover fiber =
    _ = Js.set fiber "interrupted" (Js.from True)
    _ = Js.set fiber "parked" Js.null
    _ = Js.set fiber "masks" (Js.from 0)
    if Js.read finalising && inCleanup fiber then
        cutBack fiber
    else if not (Js.to (Js.get fiber "unwinding")) then
        unwind fiber
    else
        -- Thrown out of a canceller while it cancelled its children.
        stack = Js.get fiber "stack"
        _ =
            if Js.to (Js.get stack "length") == 0 then
                Js.call stack "push" [ Js.from ended ]
            else
                Js.null
        if Js.read spawning then Js.to (Js.call stack "push" [ Js.from stopChildren ]) else ()


-- The deadline (§9.8.14 (f)): each fiber waiting inside a finaliser stops
-- waiting and goes on to its next, and from now on a finaliser runs only to
-- its first wait. A canceller that throws is reported by the host; the rest
-- go on in a new macrotask.
expire : () → ()
expire () =
    _ = Js.write deadlineTimer Js.null
    _ = Js.write expired True
    c = Js.read cleaning
    if not (Js.read finalising) || Js.isNull c then
        ()
    else
        ok = Js.ref False
        Js.finally
            (λ() →
                _ = Js.each (copy c) λfiber →
                    w = Js.get fiber "parked"
                    if Js.isNull w then
                        ()
                    else
                        _ = Js.set fiber "parked" Js.null
                        _ = enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
                        abandon fiber w
                Js.write ok True
            )
            λ() → if Js.read ok then () else macrotask (Js.from expire)


abandon : V, V → ()
abandon fiber w =
    _ = Js.set w "done" (Js.from True)
    _ = Js.write abandoned (Js.read abandoned + 1)
    _ = cutBack fiber
    canceller = Js.get w "cancel"
    if Js.isNull canceller then () else Js.to (Js.apply canceller [ Js.null ])


-- Every fiber has ended: the runtime stops for good, and `done` is told how
-- many finalisers the deadline cut short.
allEnded : () → ()
allEnded () =
    _ = Js.write phase 3
    t = Js.read deadlineTimer
    _ = if Js.isNull t then () else Js.to (Js.apply (Js.global "clearTimeout") [ t ])
    _ = Js.write deadlineTimer Js.null
    told = Js.read whenDone
    if Js.isNull told then () else Js.to (Js.apply told [ Js.from (Js.read abandoned) ])


-- ---- Masks and finalisers --------------------------------------------------

mask : () → ()
mask () =
    f = here ()
    Js.set f "masks" (Js.from (Js.to (Js.get f "masks") + 1))


unmask : a → a
unmask value =
    f = here ()
    _ = Js.set f "masks" (Js.from (Js.to (Js.get f "masks") - 1))
    value


pushFinalizer : r, (() → ()) → r
pushFinalizer resource fin =
    _ = addFinalizer (here ()) (Js.from fin)
    resource


popFinalizer : a → a
popFinalizer value =
    fins = Js.get (here ()) "finalizers"
    _ = if Js.isNull fins then () else Js.to (Js.call fins "pop" [])
    value


--| Run `body` with a scope, and when it returns, cancel every fiber it
--| started in the scope that is still running and wait for them.
--|
--|     both a b = Task.scope λs →
--|         x = Task.spawnIn s a
--|         y = Task.spawnIn s b
--|         ( Task.join x, Task.join y )
pub scope : (Scope → a) → a
scope body =
    s = openScope ()
    closeScope s (body s)


--| Run `work` where cancellation cannot reach it. A cancellation that
--| arrives meanwhile is delivered at the fiber's next suspension after it.
pub uninterruptible : (() → a) → a
uninterruptible work = unmask (work (mask ()))


--| What `restore` is handed: a way back, inside an `uninterruptibleMask`,
--| to the interruptibility there was where the mask was entered.
pub foreign type Restore


--| Run `work` where cancellation cannot reach it, as `uninterruptible`
--| does, handing it a `Restore` with which a part of it can be made
--| interruptible again: `restore token f` runs `f` as cancellable as the
--| code that entered the mask was. So a wait can be cancelled while what
--| follows it cannot — a permit taken and then always given back:
--|
--|     Task.uninterruptibleMask λtoken →
--|         permit = Task.restore token λ() → waitForPermit ()
--|         Task.onExit (λ() → Task.restore token use) λ_ → giveBack permit
--|
--| Effect's `uninterruptibleMask`. A cancellation that arrives while
--| masked is delivered at the next point where the fiber may suspend
--| inside a restored part, or after the mask.
pub uninterruptibleMask : (Restore → a) → a
uninterruptibleMask work =
    f = here ()
    token = Js.from { depth = Js.get f "masks", fiber = f, live = True }
    _ = Js.set f "masks" (Js.from (Js.to (Js.get f "masks") + 1))
    endMask token (work (Js.to token))


endMask : V, a → a
endMask token value =
    _ = Js.set token "live" (Js.from False)
    unmask value


--| Run `work` with the interruptibility there was where the mask `token`
--| came from was entered — cancellable inside a mask entered from code
--| that was, not inside one entered from an uninterruptible region — and
--| put the mask back when `work` ends. A token used after its mask has
--| returned, or by a fiber other than the one that entered it, restores
--| nothing: `work` runs as the code around it does.
pub restore : Restore, (() → b) → b
restore token work =
    t = Js.from token
    f = here ()

    if Js.to (Js.get t "live") && Js.same (Js.get t "fiber") f then
        masks = Js.get f "masks"
        _ = Js.set f "masks" (Js.get t "depth")
        remask f masks (work ())
    else
        work ()


remask : V, V, a → a
remask fiber masks value =
    _ = Js.set fiber "masks" masks
    value


--| Acquire a resource, use it, and release it however the use ends:
--| `Done` with the use's value, or `Cancelled` when the fiber was cancelled
--| during the use. Acquire and release cannot be interrupted.
--|
--|     Task.bracket (λ() → open path) (λfile _ → close file) λfile → read file
pub bracket : (() → r), (r, Exit a → ()), (r → a) → a
bracket acquire release use =
    resource = uninterruptible acquire
    result = use (pushFinalizer resource λ() → release resource Cancelled)
    uninterruptible λ() → after (release resource (Done (popFinalizer result))) result


after : (), a → a
after _ value = value


--| Run `work`, then `finally` with how it ended — `Done` with its value,
--| or `Cancelled` when the fiber was cancelled during it — where
--| cancellation cannot reach it, and answer `work`'s value. `bracket` with
--| no resource; Effect's `onExit`.
--|
--|     Task.onExit (λ() → fetch url) λexit →
--|         case exit of
--|             Done _ → Log.info "fetched"
--|             Cancelled → Log.warn "gave up"
pub onExit : (() → a), (Exit a → ()) → a
onExit work cleanup =
    result = work (pushFinalizer () λ() → cleanup Cancelled)
    uninterruptible λ() → after (cleanup (Done (popFinalizer result))) result


-- ---- Time (§17.6) ----------------------------------------------------------

--| Wait `duration` on the calling fiber's clock; only this fiber waits.
--|
--| On the real clock that is a host timer, cleared when the fiber is
--| cancelled; a wait longer than the timer's limit, 2³¹ − 1 ms, is a
--| chain of timers, so it never ends early. A `zero` wait lets every
--| other ready fiber run first, as `yieldNow` does — Effect's
--| `sleep(0)`. Inside `Clock.run` the clock is a virtual one: the fiber
--| waits until `Clock.adjust` moves that clock past the wake time, and a
--| `zero` wait returns at once.
pub sleep : Duration → ()
sleep duration =
    ms = Duration.toMillis duration
    clock = if Js.read slotted then currentClock () else Js.undefined

    if Js.isUndefined clock then
        if ms == 0 then yieldNow () else realSleep ms
    else if ms == 0 then
        ()
    else
        virtualSleep clock ms


-- The longest delay a host timer keeps: past it, both hosts fire after 1 ms.
timerLimit : Int
timerLimit = 2147483647


realSleep : Int → ()
realSleep ms =
    _ = callback λwake →
        timer =
            Js.apply (Js.global "setTimeout")
                [ Js.from λ() → Js.apply (Js.from wake) [ Js.null ]
                , Js.from (Basics.min ms timerLimit)
                ]
        λ() → Js.to (Js.apply (Js.global "clearTimeout") [ timer ])

    if ms > timerLimit then realSleep (ms - timerLimit) else ()


-- The slot record of the current fiber, or of the record outside any:
-- undefined when there is none.
slotRecord : () → V
slotRecord () =
    c = Js.read current
    src = if Js.isNull c then Js.read outside else c
    if Js.isNull src then Js.undefined else Js.get src "slots"


--| The calling fiber's clock slot (§17.5): undefined for the real clock, or
--| a clock `virtualClock` made. For core's `Clock`, which is what a program
--| calls; the `Js.Value` it answers is of no use anywhere else.
pub currentClock : () → Js.Value
currentClock () =
    if Js.read slotted then
        r = slotRecord ()
        if Js.isNullish r then Js.undefined else Js.get r "clock"
    else
        Js.undefined


--| Run `work` with the calling fiber's clock slot set to `clock`, and put
--| the old one back when `work` ends, returned or cancelled. Fibers `work`
--| starts copy it. For core's `Clock.run`: a program has no `Js.Value` to
--| give it.
pub withClock : Js.Value, (() → a) → a
withClock clock work =
    _ = Js.write slotted True
    fiber = here ()
    old = Js.get fiber "slots"
    next = Js.call (Js.global "Object") "assign" [ Js.from {}, old ]
    _ = Js.set next "clock" clock
    _ = Js.set fiber "slots" next
    putSlots fiber old (work (pushFinalizer () λ() → Js.set fiber "slots" old))


putSlots : V, V, a → a
putSlots fiber old value =
    _ = popFinalizer ()
    _ = Js.set fiber "slots" old
    value


-- ---- The virtual clock (§17.6) ---------------------------------------------

--| A virtual clock reading `epoch` milliseconds, with no sleepers: what
--| core's `Clock.virtual` makes. A program has no `Js.Value` to give it.
pub virtualClock : Js.Value → Js.Value
virtualClock epoch = Js.from { now = epoch, sleepers = Js.array [] }


-- Wait on the virtual clock `clock` until it reads `ms` later than now.
-- Sleepers are kept ordered by wake time, and by the order they began to
-- sleep among equal times; a cancelled one is taken out.
virtualSleep : V, Int → ()
virtualSleep clock ms = callback λwake →
    at : Int
    at = Js.to (Js.get clock "now") + ms
    entry = Js.from { at = at, wake = Js.from wake }
    sleepers = Js.get clock "sleepers"
    _ = Js.call sleepers "splice" [ Js.from (insertAt sleepers at 0), Js.from 0, entry ]

    λ() →
        i : Int
        i = Js.to (Js.call sleepers "indexOf" [ entry ])
        if i ≥ 0 then Js.to (Js.call sleepers "splice" [ Js.from i, Js.from 1 ]) else ()


-- Where a sleeper waking at `at` goes: after every one waking at or before.
insertAt : V, Int, Int → Int
insertAt sleepers at i =
    if i < Js.to (Js.get sleepers "length") && Js.to (Js.get (Js.at sleepers i) "at") ≤ at then
        insertAt sleepers at (i + 1)
    else
        i


--| Move the virtual clock `clock` forward by `ms` milliseconds (a
--| `Js.Value`), and return once everything that woke has run as far as it
--| can: core's `Clock.adjust`.
--|
--| It first lets every other ready fiber run until none is (*settles*);
--| then, while the earliest sleeper is due by the target, sets the reading
--| to its wake time, wakes every sleeper due then, in the order they began
--| to sleep, and settles again — so a sleeper the woken code registers is
--| woken too if it is due by the target. Last, the reading is the target.
pub adjustClock : Js.Value, Js.Value → ()
adjustClock clock ms =
    by : Int
    by = Js.to ms

    if by ≤ 0 then
        ()
    else
        _ = settle ()
        advance clock (Js.to (Js.get clock "now") + by)


advance : V, Int → ()
advance clock target =
    sleepers = Js.get clock "sleepers"

    if Js.to (Js.get sleepers "length") > 0 && Js.to (Js.get (Js.at sleepers 0) "at") ≤ target then
        at : Int
        at = Js.to (Js.get (Js.at sleepers 0) "at")
        _ = Js.set clock "now" (Js.from at)
        _ = wakeDue sleepers at
        _ = settle ()
        advance clock target
    else
        Js.set clock "now" (Js.from target)


wakeDue : V, Int → ()
wakeDue sleepers at =
    if Js.to (Js.get sleepers "length") > 0 && Js.to (Js.get (Js.at sleepers 0) "at") == at then
        entry = Js.call sleepers "shift" []
        _ = Js.apply (Js.get entry "wake") [ Js.null ]
        wakeDue sleepers at
    else
        ()


-- Let every other fiber that is ready run, again and again, until none is:
-- the scheduler's queue holds nothing but what the caller left there.
settle : () → ()
settle () =
    if Js.to (Js.get queue "length") > Js.read head then
        _ = yieldNow ()
        settle ()
    else
        ()


-- ---- Retrying and repeating (§17.8) ----------------------------------------

--| Run `work`; an `Ok` is the answer at once. On an `Err`, step `policy`
--| with it: `Stop` makes that `Err` the answer, and `Continue` sleeps its
--| delay on the calling fiber's clock and runs `work` again, stepping the
--| next schedule after that. A cancelled `work` never returns, so it is
--| never retried. Effect's `retry`.
--|
--|     -- at most four runs, 100, 200 and 400 ms apart
--|     Task.retry (Schedule.max (Schedule.exponential (Duration.millis 100) 2.0) (Schedule.recurs 3)) fetch
pub retry : Schedule e, (() → Result e a) → Result e a
retry policy work = retryFrom policy work (clockMillis ()) 1


retryFrom : Schedule e, (() → Result e a), Int, Int → Result e a
retryFrom policy work began attempt =
    case work () of
        Ok value →
            Ok value

        Err problem →
            case Schedule.step policy (metadata problem attempt began) of
                Schedule.Stop →
                    Err problem

                Schedule.Continue delay next →
                    _ = sleep delay
                    retryFrom next work began (attempt + 1)


--| Run `work`, step `policy` with its value, and while it continues
--| sleep its delay and run `work` again; the last value is the answer.
--| `repeat (Schedule.recurs 2)` runs `work` three times. Effect's `repeat`.
pub repeat : Schedule a, (() → a) → a
repeat policy work = repeatFrom policy work (clockMillis ()) 1


repeatFrom : Schedule a, (() → a), Int, Int → a
repeatFrom policy work began attempt =
    value = work ()

    case Schedule.step policy (metadata value attempt began) of
        Schedule.Stop →
            value

        Schedule.Continue delay next →
            _ = sleep delay
            repeatFrom next work began (attempt + 1)


-- One step's metadata: the time since `began` on the calling fiber's clock,
-- and a random draw — from the host, until a seed slot is set (§17.5; the
-- seed is P9's `Random.withSeed`, which nothing writes yet).
metadata : i, Int, Int → Schedule.Metadata i
metadata input attempt began =
    { input = input
    , attempt = attempt
    , elapsed = Duration.millis (clockMillis () - began)
    , random = Js.to (Js.call (Js.global "Math") "random" [])
    }


-- The epoch milliseconds of the calling fiber's clock (core's `Clock.now`).
clockMillis : () → Int
clockMillis () =
    clock = if Js.read slotted then currentClock () else Js.undefined

    if Js.isUndefined clock then
        Js.to (Js.call (Js.global "Date") "now" [])
    else
        Js.to (Js.get clock "now")


-- ---- Structured combinators (§17.7) ----------------------------------------
--
-- Each runs its branches as children in a scope of its own, so it returns —
-- or is cancelled — only after every child it started has ended and run its
-- cleanup (§17.1 item 2). They wait on the kernel's observers directly
-- (`firstOf`), not on a `Deferred`, which is a module above this one.

-- Park until one of `fibers`, a JavaScript array, has ended with an outcome
-- `stop` holds of, and answer it; or until every one has ended, and answer
-- null. At once when that is already so; the fibers are looked at in array
-- order.
firstOf : V, (V → Bool) → V
firstOf fibers stop =
    found = endedWith fibers stop 0

    if not (Js.isNull found) then
        found
    else if allDone fibers 0 then
        Js.null
    else
        each = Js.ref Js.null

        got = suspend λwake →
            left = Js.ref 0
            _ = Js.each fibers λf →
                if Js.isNull (Js.get f "outcome") then Js.write left (Js.read left + 1) else ()

            observer = Js.from λf →
                _ = Js.write left (Js.read left - 1)

                if stop (Js.get f "outcome") then
                    Js.to (Js.apply wake [ f ])
                else if Js.read left == 0 then
                    Js.to (Js.apply wake [ Js.null ])
                else
                    ()
            _ = Js.write each observer
            _ = Js.each fibers λf →
                if Js.isNull (Js.get f "outcome") then observe f observer else ()
            Js.from λ_ → Js.each fibers λf → unobserve f observer
        _ = Js.each fibers λf → unobserve f (Js.read each)
        got


endedWith : V, (V → Bool), Int → V
endedWith fibers stop i =
    if i ≥ Js.to (Js.get fibers "length") then
        Js.null
    else
        f = Js.at fibers i
        o = Js.get f "outcome"
        if not (Js.isNull o) && stop o then f else endedWith fibers stop (i + 1)


allDone : V, Int → Bool
allDone fibers i =
    if i ≥ Js.to (Js.get fibers "length") then
        True
    else if Js.isNull (Js.get (Js.at fibers i) "outcome") then
        False
    else
        allDone fibers (i + 1)


-- Whether an outcome is `Cancelled`.
wasCancelled : V → Bool
wasCancelled o =
    case guest o of
        Done _ →
            False

        Cancelled →
            True


-- Whether an outcome is `Done`.
wasDone : V → Bool
wasDone o = not (wasCancelled o)


-- Whether an outcome is `Done (Err _)` or `Cancelled`: what ends a
-- fail-fast combinator.
failedOrCancelled : V → Bool
failedOrCancelled o =
    case guest o of
        Done (Err _) →
            True

        Done (Ok _) →
            False

        Cancelled →
            True


-- Whether an outcome is `Done (Ok _)`.
succeeded : V → Bool
succeeded o =
    case guest o of
        Done (Ok _) →
            True

        _ →
            False


-- The value of a fiber that ended `Done`.
valueOf : V → a
valueOf f =
    case guest (Js.get f "outcome") of
        Done v →
            v

        Cancelled →
            selfCancel ()


-- Wait for `fibers` to end, or for one to end `Cancelled` by itself — when
-- the caller is cancelled too, and the scope cancels and awaits the rest.
allOrCancel : V → ()
allOrCancel fibers =
    stopped = firstOf fibers wasCancelled
    if Js.isNull stopped then () else selfCancel ()


--| Run both concurrently, and answer both values, in argument order. If
--| one of them is cancelled — it joined a cancelled fiber — the other is
--| cancelled and waited for, and so is the caller. Effect's `all` of two.
pub par : (() → a), (() → b) → a × b
par a b = within λs →
    fa = startIn s a
    fb = startIn s b
    _ = allOrCancel (Js.array [ fa, fb ])
    ( valueOf fa, valueOf fb )


--| `par` of three.
pub par3 : (() → a), (() → b), (() → c) → a × b × c
par3 a b c = within λs →
    fa = startIn s a
    fb = startIn s b
    fc = startIn s c
    _ = allOrCancel (Js.array [ fa, fb, fc ])
    ( valueOf fa, valueOf fb, valueOf fc )


--| Run both concurrently; the first `Err` to arrive cancels the other,
--| waits for its cleanup, and is the answer. `Ok` of both values, in
--| argument order, otherwise. Effect's `all`, which fails fast.
pub parOk : (() → Result e a), (() → Result e b) → Result e (a × b)
parOk a b = within λs →
    fa = startIn s a
    fb = startIn s b
    stopped = firstOf (Js.array [ fa, fb ]) failedOrCancelled

    if Js.isNull stopped then
        case ( valueOf fa, valueOf fb ) of
            ( Ok x, Ok y ) →
                Ok ( x, y )

            ( Err why, _ ) →
                Err why

            ( _, Err why ) →
                Err why
    else
        case valueOf stopped of
            Err why →
                Err why

            Ok _ →
                selfCancel ()


-- The elements of a list, as a JavaScript array.
arrayOf : List a → V
arrayOf xs = List.foldl xs (Js.array []) λx arr →
    _ = Js.call arr "push" [ Js.from x ]
    arr


--| Call `f` on every element, at most `bound` calls running at once — each
--| started, in list order, as one before it ends — and answer the results
--| in list order. A `bound` below 1 is 1; `List.length xs` runs them all at
--| once. If a call is cancelled, no more are started, those running are
--| cancelled and waited for, and the caller is cancelled. Effect's
--| `forEach` with `concurrency`.
pub forEach : List a, Int, (a → b) → List b
forEach xs bound f =
    items = arrayOf xs
    results = Js.array []

    stopped = within λh →
        bounded h items results (Basics.max 1 bound) (Js.from f) (λ_ → False) wasCancelled

    if Js.isNull stopped then
        List.initialize (Js.to (Js.get items "length")) λi → Js.to (Js.at results i)
    else
        selfCancel ()


--| `forEach` for a function that answers a `Result`: on the first `Err`,
--| no more calls are started, those running are cancelled and waited for,
--| and that `Err` is the answer. `Ok` of every result, in list order,
--| otherwise.
pub forEachOk : List a, Int, (a → Result e b) → Result e (List b)
forEachOk xs bound f =
    items = arrayOf xs
    results = Js.array []

    stopped = within λh →
        bounded h items results (Basics.max 1 bound) (Js.from f) isErr failedOrCancelled

    if Js.isNull stopped then
        Ok (List.initialize (Js.to (Js.get items "length")) λi → okValue (Js.at results i))
    else
        case valueOf stopped of
            Err why →
                Err why

            Ok _ →
                selfCancel ()


-- Whether a call's value is an `Err`.
isErr : V → Bool
isErr v =
    case Js.to v of
        Err _ →
            True

        Ok _ →
            False


-- What `forEachOk` stored for a call that answered `Ok`.
okValue : V → b
okValue v =
    case Js.to v of
        Ok b →
            b

        Err _ →
            Js.to Js.null


-- Run `call` on every item, at most `bound` at once, the values into
-- `results` at their items' indices. Stop at the first call whose value
-- `stopsAt` holds of, or whose fiber's outcome `ends` does, and answer that
-- fiber (a record of the outcome, for a call that ended at once) — or null
-- once every call has ended.
bounded : V, V, V, Int, V, (V → Bool), (V → Bool) → V
bounded h items results bound call stopsAt ends =
    boundedFrom h items results bound call stopsAt ends 0 (Js.array []) (Js.array [])


boundedFrom : V, V, V, Int, V, (V → Bool), (V → Bool), Int, V, V → V
boundedFrom h items results bound call stopsAt ends next inFlight slots =
    if Js.to (Js.get inFlight "length") < bound && next < Js.to (Js.get items "length") then
        r = begin h call (Js.at items next)
        fiber = Js.read started

        -- A call that ended at once is never in flight.
        if not (Js.isNull fiber) then
            _ = Js.call inFlight "push" [ fiber ]
            _ = Js.call slots "push" [ Js.from next ]
            boundedFrom h items results bound call stopsAt ends (next + 1) inFlight slots
        else if stopsAt r then
            Js.from { outcome = host (Done (guest r)) }
        else
            _ = Js.setAt results next r
            boundedFrom h items results bound call stopsAt ends (next + 1) inFlight slots
    else if Js.to (Js.get inFlight "length") == 0 then
        Js.null
    else
        _ = firstOf inFlight λ_ → True
        stop = harvest inFlight slots results ends 0
        if Js.isNull stop then
            boundedFrom h items results bound call stopsAt ends next inFlight slots
        else
            stop


-- Take the fibers of `inFlight` that have ended out of it, their values into
-- `results` at their slots; answer the first whose outcome `ends` holds of,
-- or null.
harvest : V, V, V, (V → Bool), Int → V
harvest inFlight slots results ends i =
    if i ≥ Js.to (Js.get inFlight "length") then
        Js.null
    else
        f = Js.at inFlight i
        o = Js.get f "outcome"

        if Js.isNull o then
            harvest inFlight slots results ends (i + 1)
        else if ends o then
            f
        else
            _ = Js.setAt results (Js.to (Js.at slots i)) (doneValue o)
            _ = Js.call inFlight "splice" [ Js.from i, Js.from 1 ]
            _ = Js.call slots "splice" [ Js.from i, Js.from 1 ]
            harvest inFlight slots results ends i


-- The value in a `Done` outcome, as a JavaScript one.
doneValue : V → V
doneValue o =
    case guest o of
        Done v →
            Js.from v

        Cancelled →
            Js.null


--| Run both concurrently; the first to return is the answer, and the other
--| is cancelled and waited for — its cleanup has run — before it is
--| returned. A branch cancelled by itself never wins; if both are, the
--| caller is cancelled. Effect's `raceFirst`.
pub race : (() → a), (() → a) → a
race a b = raceAll a [ b ]


--| `race` of any number of branches, `first` and then `rest`: the first to
--| return wins, and every other branch is cancelled and waited for before
--| the answer is returned. Effect's `raceAllFirst`.
pub raceAll : (() → a), List (() → a) → a
raceAll first rest = within λs →
    fibers = arrayOf (List.map [ first, …rest ] λt → startIn s t)
    winner = firstOf fibers wasDone
    if Js.isNull winner then selfCancel () else valueOf winner


--| The first branch to answer `Ok` wins, and the rest are cancelled and
--| waited for; an `Err` does not end the race. When no branch answers
--| `Ok`, the answer is `Err` of every branch's error, in argument order —
--| a branch cancelled by itself gives none, and if every branch was, the
--| caller is cancelled. No branches at all is `Err []`. Effect's `race`.
pub raceOk : List (() → Result e a) → Result (List e) a
raceOk thunks =
    if List.isEmpty thunks then
        Err []
    else
        within λs →
            fibers = List.map thunks λt → startIn s t
            winner = firstOf (arrayOf fibers) succeeded

            if Js.isNull winner then
                errors = List.filterMap fibers λf → errorOf (Js.get (Js.from f) "outcome")
                if List.isEmpty errors then selfCancel () else Err errors
            else
                case valueOf winner of
                    Ok v →
                        Ok v

                    Err _ →
                        selfCancel ()


errorOf : V → Maybe e
errorOf o =
    case guest o of
        Done (Err why) →
            Just why

        _ →
            Nothing


--| Run `work`; if it returns before `duration` has passed on the calling
--| fiber's clock, `Just` its value. Otherwise `work` is cancelled, its
--| cleanup waited for, and the answer is `Nothing` — so `timeout` may take
--| longer than `duration`, by as long as that cleanup takes, and `work`
--| that cannot be interrupted when the time passes runs to its next point
--| of suspension first. A `zero` duration answers `Nothing` without
--| starting `work`. Effect's `timeoutOption`.
--|
--|     Task.timeout (Duration.seconds 5) (λ() → Http.get url)
--|         ▷ Maybe.withDefault (Err Http.Timeout)
pub timeout : Duration, (() → a) → Maybe a
timeout duration work =
    if Duration.toMillis duration == 0 then
        Nothing
    else
        within λs →
            child = startIn s work

            -- Work that answered without waiting needs no timer.
            if not (Js.isNull (Js.get child "outcome")) then
                Just (valueOf child)
            else
                timer = startIn s λ() → sleep duration
                first = firstOf (Js.array [ child, timer ]) λ_ → True
                if Js.same first child then Just (valueOf child) else Nothing


-- How a combinator starts a child (§17.7's amendment, *How a combinator
-- starts its children*): at once, inside the call, the child's work called
-- with the child as the current fiber — as Effect forks a combinator's
-- children with `startImmediately`. Core-private: no program can ask for
-- it.
--
-- `begin h work arg` calls `work` with `arg`. Work that returns without
-- suspending, and leaves no child of its own running, has simply ended: its
-- value is the answer, `started` is null, and the fiber it ran as was never
-- listed in the scope, queued or counted — so the holder keeps it, as
-- `probe`, for the next child to run as. Work that suspends becomes a fiber
-- of the holder's scope like any other, its continuations on its stack,
-- parked where it parked: `started` is that fiber, and the answer null.
begin : V, V, V → V
begin h work arg =
    probe = Js.get h "probe"

    fiber =
        if Js.isNull probe then
            parent = Js.read current
            made = newFiber parent (Js.array [])
            _ = if Js.read slotted then Js.set made "slots" (slotsOf parent) else ()
            made
        else
            probe

    if Js.read phase ≠ 0 then
        -- Cancelled before it runs, as `spawnIn` would.
        _ = Js.set h "probe" Js.null
        _ =
            Js.call (Js.get fiber "stack") "push"
                [ Js.from finish, Js.from λ_ → Js.apply work [ arg ] ]
        _ = enlist h fiber
        _ = Js.set fiber "interrupted" (Js.from True)
        _ = enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
        _ = Js.write started fiber
        Js.null
    else
        r = callAs fiber h work arg

        if Js.same r sentinel then
            -- It suspended: what the run loop does when a resumption parks.
            _ = Js.set h "probe" Js.null
            _ = enlist h fiber
            p = Js.read pending
            _ = Js.write pending Js.null
            stack = Js.get fiber "stack"
            _ = Js.call stack "push" [ Js.from finish ]
            ks = Js.get p "ks"
            _ = takeOn stack ks (Js.to (Js.get ks "length") - 1)

            _ =
                if Js.to (Js.get p "interrupt") then
                    _ = unwind fiber
                    enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
                else
                    Js.set fiber "parked" (Js.get p "wait")
            _ = Js.write started fiber
            Js.null
        else if not (Js.read spawning) || none (Js.get fiber "children") then
            _ = Js.set h "probe" fiber
            _ = Js.write started Js.null
            r
        else
            -- It started children of its own, still running: its end
            -- cancels and waits for them, in a fiber like any other.
            _ = Js.set h "probe" Js.null
            _ = enlist h fiber
            _ = Js.call (Js.get fiber "stack") "push" [ Js.from finish, Js.from λ_ → r ]
            _ = enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
            _ = Js.write started fiber
            Js.null


-- The fiber the last `begin` left running, or null when its work ended at
-- once.
started : Js.Ref V
started = Js.ref Js.null


-- `begin` of a thunk, answering a fiber either way: the running one, or a
-- record of the ended one's outcome, which is all a combinator reads of a
-- child that has ended.
startIn : V, (() → a) → V
startIn h work =
    r = begin h (Js.from work) Js.null
    f = Js.read started
    if Js.isNull f then Js.from { outcome = host (Done (guest r)) } else f


-- List `fiber`, still running, in the scope the holder `h` keeps — opened
-- now, on the current fiber, if this is the first child that needs one.
enlist : V, V → ()
enlist h fiber =
    known = Js.get h "sc"

    s =
        if Js.isNull known then
            opened = Js.from (openScope ())
            _ = Js.set h "sc" opened
            opened
        else
            known
    _ = Js.write live (Js.read live + 1)
    _ = Js.set fiber "scope" s
    Js.to (Js.call (Js.get s "children") "add" [ fiber ])


-- Run a combinator's `body` with a holder for its children, `{ probe, sc }`:
-- the fiber the next child runs as, and the scope children still running
-- belong to — opened only when one is (`enlist`), and closed, its fibers
-- cancelled and awaited, when `body` returns, as `scope` closes its own.
-- Children that all end at once cost one fiber record and no scope.
within : (V → a) → a
within body =
    h = Js.from { probe = Js.null, sc = Js.null }
    closeHeld h (body h)


closeHeld : V, a → a
closeHeld h value =
    sc = Js.get h "sc"
    if Js.isNull sc then value else closeScope (Js.to sc) value


-- Call `work` with `arg` and `fiber` as the current fiber, and answer what
-- it returned, the sentinel included. If it throws — a defect — the throw
-- goes on to the host as it would from the drain, but the fiber that was
-- running here is put back as the current one first, so the drain's guard
-- takes it for the culprit, and `fiber` is listed in its scope, set on the
-- road to its end and queued, so the culprit's cleanup reaches it. Nothing
-- is caught (`CLAUDE.md` rule 9).
callAs : V, V, V, V → V
callAs fiber h work arg =
    outer = Js.read current
    _ = Js.write current fiber
    ok = Js.ref False

    r =
        Js.finally
            (λ() →
                v = Js.apply work [ arg ]
                _ = Js.write ok True
                v
            )
            λ() →
                _ = Js.write current outer

                if Js.read ok then
                    ()
                else
                    _ = Js.write pending Js.null
                    _ = Js.set h "probe" Js.null
                    _ = enlist h fiber
                    _ = recover fiber
                    enqueue fiber Js.null Js.null
    r


-- `pushBack`, for `begin`: a copy, so that in a build that reaches a
-- combinator, where the run loop and `begin` both live, each has a loop of
-- its own written in place, and the run loop pays no call per park
-- (`backend.md` §9, *A function called once …*, amended 2026-10-02, has
-- the measurements). A build that reaches no combinator writes the same
-- bytes either way.
takeOn : V, V, Int → ()
takeOn stack ks i =
    if i < 0 then
        ()
    else
        _ = Js.call stack "push" [ Js.at ks i ]
        takeOn stack ks (i - 1)
